The most interesting (or rather fundamental) part of information
about a level is where the stairs are. Not knowing that means you
have to perform a boring investigation/exploration in every maze
(and this is even more boring if you have no source of light).

As soon as you have that information you have a lot of options;
use wands or pickaxes to dig a direct connection, use controlled
teleport reach the stairs, or even uncontrolled teleport to come
closer at least, or decide to use other means to leave the level
(up: cursed gain level, down: digging).

Note aside: I find tame and hostile umber hulks especially helpful.
Wait for hostiles to dig paths to you, then teleport away (even
teleporting randomly is often helpful), rinse repeat. Opens short
paths throughout the level. Keep tame ones close to you as a fast
pickaxe substitute.

